From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350: fix the IPA interrupt

The IPA interrupt on SM8350 is GIC SPI 654, not 655. The downstream
lahaina device tree uses 654 for its "ipa-irq", and so does every
other SoC here that has the GSI interrupt on SPI 432 (sc7280, sm8550,
sm8650, milos).

Data still flows on 655, because RX completions arrive on the GSI
interrupt, so the wrong line goes unnoticed. What is lost is
everything the IPA interrupt carries: the microcontroller never gets
its INIT_COMPLETED response through, so the IPA keeps the proxy power
reference ipa_uc_power() took and never runtime-suspends, and
TX_SUSPEND never reaches the AP, so modem data cannot wake the system
from suspend. On a phone that means incoming calls and SMS wait until
something else wakes it.

Fixes: f11d3e7da32e ("arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350: add IPA information")
Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi
@@ -1845,7 +1845,7 @@
 				    "ipa-shared",
 				    "gsi";
 
-			interrupts-extended = <&intc GIC_SPI 655 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+			interrupts-extended = <&intc GIC_SPI 654 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
 					      <&intc GIC_SPI 432 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 					      <&ipa_smp2p_in 0 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
 					      <&ipa_smp2p_in 1 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
